# File: tests/features/model-hub.feature
# Generated from: specs/31-fix-clinepass-http-400-on-paid-models-and-arrow-key-navigation-in-the-model-hub/requirements.md
Feature: ClinePass requests name listed ids, and the hub navigates with the arrows

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A paid ClinePass model is requested with its listed id
    Given a ClinePass login and a catalog entry "cline-pass/qwen3.7-plus" cached with the model "qwen3.7-plus"
    When a routed step runs on "cline-pass/qwen3.7-plus"
    Then the request names "cline-pass/qwen3.7-plus"

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A free ClinePass model is requested as listed
    Given a ClinePass catalog entry "cline-pass/cline-free/solar-mini4"
    When a routed step runs on it
    Then the request names "cline-free/solar-mini4"

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: The arrows move through the models
    Given the hub is open
    When the person presses down and then left
    Then the models selection moves, the pane does not scroll, and the session stays where it is

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: The providers stay visible and selectable
    Given the hub was scrolled and closed
    When the person opens the hub again, presses Tab, chooses "OpenCode Go" and presses Enter
    Then every provider shows in the sidebar, the models list shows OpenCode Go's models, and the ring is on the models

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Enter switches to the chosen model
    Given "haiku" is selected in the models list
    When the person presses Enter
    Then the hub closes and "/model haiku" runs
